expected_issues.description:
Missing null validation: The constructor doesn't validate if the `purposes` parameter or its elements are null. This could lead to NullReferenceException when calling `GetByteCount` or `GetBytes`. Consider adding validation at the beginning of the constructor:

```csharp
ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(purposes);
for (int i = 0; i < purposes.Length; i++)
{
    ArgumentNullException.ThrowIfNull(purposes[i], $"purposes[{i}]");
}
```

Or at minimum, add Debug.Assert statements similar to the original implementation.

